# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD starts rabbitmq-server in the background, waits for the
# management API (15672) to come up, then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the broker is ALREADY RUNNING with the default guest/guest account when
#     the agent starts (the vulnerability is live);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, not the broker, so management actions cannot
#     kill the container.
#
# The remediation here is a RUNTIME change (rabbitmqctl delete_user guest), so
# there is no "forgot to restart" case - deleting the user takes effect
# immediately on the live broker.
